### 2. `bro run` — Command Shortcuts

**Two modes of invocation:**

```
# Mode 1: Fuzzy search (interactive)
$ bro run
┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
│ > _                                  │
│   connect-db-staging    Connect to staging postgres    │
│   connect-db-prod       Connect to prod postgres       │
│   gcp-auth              Auth to GCP project            │
│   k8s-staging           Switch to staging k8s context  │
│   docker-clean          Prune all docker resources     │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
# Arrow keys to navigate, enter to execute, type to filter

# Mode 2: Direct alias
$ bro run gcp-auth
$ bro run connect-db --preset staging
```

**How it works:**

1. Loads shortcuts from both global config (`~/.bro/commands.yaml`) and project-level config (`.bro.yaml` in repo root)
2. Project-level commands take precedence and appear first in the list
3. In interactive mode, presents a scrollable/filterable list using arrow keys
4. On selection, executes the command in the user's current shell context
5. Supports parameterized commands with `{{placeholder}}` syntax — prompts for values at runtime or uses configured defaults/presets

**Shortcut definition:**

```yaml
shortcuts:
  connect-db:
    description: "Connect to postgres database"
    command: "psql -h {{host}} -U {{user}} -d {{db}}"
    defaults:
      user: "dev"
      db: "app"
    presets:
      staging:
        host: "staging.db.internal"
      prod:
        host: "prod.db.internal"
        user: "readonly"

  gcp-auth:
    description: "Authenticate to GCP project"
    command: "gcloud auth login && gcloud config set project {{project_id}}"
    defaults:
      project_id: "my-project-123"

  docker-clean:
    description: "Prune all Docker resources"
    command: "docker system prune -af && docker volume prune -f"
```

