## Configuration

### File Locations

```
~/.bro/
├── config.yaml           # Main configuration
├── commands.yaml          # Global command shortcuts
├── standups/              # Generated standup summaries
│   ├── 2026-02-13.md
│   └── 2026-02-14.md
└── templates/             # Custom commit message templates (if any)
```

Per-project config: `.bro.yaml` at the repo root (optional, for project-specific shortcuts and profile overrides).

### Main Config (`~/.bro/config.yaml`)

```yaml
# LLM Configuration
llm:
  provider: "anthropic"       # "anthropic" | "openai"
  anthropic:
    api_key: "sk-ant-..."     # or set via BRO_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY env var
    model: "claude-sonnet-4-20250514"
  openai:
    api_key: "sk-..."         # or set via BRO_OPENAI_API_KEY env var
    model: "gpt-4o"

# Commit Profiles
profiles:
  org:
    commit_template: "{project}-{ticket} #comment {message}"
    branch_pattern: "^(?P<project>[A-Z]+)-(?P<ticket>\\d+)"
    llm_instructions: "Keep commit messages concise, imperative mood, under 72 chars"
  personal:
    commit_style: "conventional"
    llm_instructions: "Use conventional commit format. Determine the type from the diff."

# Directory → Profile mapping
projects:
  "~/work/*": "org"
  "~/personal/*": "personal"

# Standup Configuration
standup:
  repos:
    - ~/work/backend
    - ~/work/frontend
    - ~/personal/*
  author: "Your Name"
  output_dir: "~/.bro/standups"
  lookback: "auto"

# General
editor: ""                 # defaults to $EDITOR
```

### Setup Wizard

First-time run (`k` with no args or `k init`) launches an interactive setup:

1. Choose LLM provider
2. Enter API key (stored in config, with recommendation to use env var instead)
3. Set up a default profile
4. Optionally configure standup repos

