## Distribution

### `go install`

```bash
go install github.com/<username>/k@latest
```

### Homebrew

Create a separate repo `homebrew-bro` with a formula:

```ruby
class K < Formula
  desc "Developer productivity CLI — smart commits, command shortcuts, standup summaries"
  homepage "https://github.com/<username>/k"
  url "https://github.com/<username>/k/releases/download/v0.1.0/k_0.1.0_darwin_arm64.tar.gz"
  sha256 "..."

  def install
    bin.install "bro"
  end
end
```

Install via:

```bash
brew tap <username>/bro
brew install bro
```

Homebrew taps are completely free — just a GitHub repo with the formula file. Use GoReleaser to automate building binaries for each release and updating the formula.

